# E §5 step 1 under a hole law date (tally 2.3, #247; P10, H2): a1 and a2 state `amt`, which pay's leg
# reads, so each adjustment is the hole, its δ too: `where a.change > big` over them is the hole. Before: 0
# (a per-day δ of 50.00 PLN and 10.00 PLN, never above big).
=== m.tally
model b2c
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input big: money PLN
input w: date
input dd: date
move pay: transfers
  on dd
  at w
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-05) "s"
  dd = 2026-03-10 "s"
  big = 70.00 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
version a0
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
version a1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-20
  replace amt = 150.00 PLN "s"
version a2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-04-10
  replace amt = 160.00 PLN "s"
ask wb: count(a in adjustments over .. where a.change > big)
ask wb_p03: count(a in adjustments over .. where a.change > big) with w = 2026-03-03
=== expect
wb: ?"date within window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-05) not precise enough for the law date of pay" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-06-10
wb_p03: 0
  pinned: w = 2026-03-03
  cut 2026-06-10
